[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3059204136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3059204136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3059204136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62V8Ao","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T21:45:54Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T21:45:54Z","body":"I'm opening a draft PR tonight just to validate the approach given that it lengthens the code a bunch (many tags were not accounted for in the existing implementation) before spending time testing and refining it on one of my next days off. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3059204136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3060731890","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3060731890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3060731890,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62bw_y","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T06:06:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T06:06:21Z","body":"The approach seems fine to me. We won't get less code with a parser/scanner I think. Just curious whether we can solve `[lb]`/`[rb]` using it. But I think some edge cases are fine for now, since this is clearly an overall improvement.\r\n\r\n> I used this page from the documentation as a reference: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_documentation_comments.html#doc-gdscript-documentation-comments-bbcode-and-class-reference\r\n\r\nNote that the class ref uses an alternative undocumented syntax for it's multi language code blocks:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[codeblocks]\r\n[gdscript]\r\n[/gdscript]\r\n[/codeblocks]\r\n```\r\n\r\nNo clue why, but that's how it is right now iirc.\r\n\r\n> * **Strikethrough:** I went with `~~` which one of the two supported [GitHub flavored markdown syntax](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/writing-on-github/getting-started-with-writing-and-formatting-on-github/basic-writing-and-formatting-syntax). I tried using html tags but they're not supported in some code editors.\r\n\r\nThat's fine, the LSP spec specifically says: \"If the format is markdown the content should follow the [GitHub Flavored Markdown Specification](https://github.github.com/gfm/).\"\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3060731890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3061971123","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3061971123","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3061971123,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62gfiz","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T11:45:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T11:45:20Z","body":"> The approach seems fine to me. We won't get less code with a parser/scanner I think. Just curious whether we can solve [lb]/[rb] using it. But I think some edge cases are fine for now, since this is clearly an overall improvement.\r\n\r\nSure, we can! We just need to move up the class search and replace and specifically add exceptions for the pattern \"[lb|rb]\", and finally replace those last after everything has been processed. It should do the trick.\r\n\r\nThanks for the confirmation and feedback; yes, a scanner tokenizer + rendering to strings would easily take double the lines of code.\r\n\r\nNext time I'll address the missing things, test, and properly format and squash everything (likely on Monday night).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3061971123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3089878756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3089878756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3089878756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64K87k","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-18T15:36:03Z","updated_at":"2025-07-18T15:42:31Z","body":"Sorry for the delay. I actually ended up not having the time to get back to this earlier. I just took the time to correct most issues, test the documentation, and format.\r\n\r\nFor replacing literal brackets aka [lb] and [rb] I went with folding them into the while loop that looks for class names: if the literal bracket patterns are found, they're immediately replaced and we advance past the replaced literal bracket. It ensures they won't conflict with classname search and replace. Other patterns look for specific keywords so it should be good enough.\r\n\r\n## Remaining codeblocks syntax search and replace - needs feedback and decision\r\n\r\nThere's just one thing I would need feedback on to decide how to handle it: the special multi language code listings. E.g.:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n## [codeblocks]\r\n## [gdscript]\r\n## print(hash(\"a\")) # Prints 177670\r\n## [/gdscript]\r\n## [csharp]\r\n## GD.Print(GD.Hash(\"a\")); // Prints 177670\r\n## [/csharp]\r\n## [/codeblocks]\r\n```\r\n\r\nAn issue with the markdown parsing in code editors through the language server is that it seems fenced code blocks with a language are not supported. I will just get a literal \\`\\`\\`gdscript if I try outputting that. That's why code blocks indent every line in the original code.\r\n\r\nOne way to output the codeblocks example above would be:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\nGDScript:\r\n    print(hash(\"a\")) # Prints 177670\r\nC#:\r\n    GD.Print(GD.Hash(\"a\")); // Prints 177670\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis should produce a documentation popup with content like this in external editors:\r\n\r\n> GDScript:\r\n> ```\r\n> print(hash(\"a\")) # Prints 177670\r\n> ```\r\n> C#:\r\n> ```\r\n> GD.Print(GD.Hash(\"a\")); // Prints 177670\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nWhat do you think? Let me know if there's any particular output you'd like and I'll implement that to complete the feature.\r\n\r\n## Current state of the PR\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n  <summary>Here is the test docstring I'm using to try to cover as many bits of syntax as possible:</summary>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n## [b]TestDocs[/b] - A comprehensive documentation test class.[br]\r\n##\r\n## This class demonstrates [i]all[/i] available BBCode tags and links:[br]\r\n## [br]\r\n## - Class link: [Node2D], [Sprite2D], [RigidBody2D][br]\r\n## - Method link: [method Node2D.set_position], [method Node.get_name][br]\r\n## - Property link: [member Node2D.position], [member Node2D.scale][br]\r\n## - Signal link: [signal Node.ready], [signal Node.renamed][br]\r\n## - Constant link: [constant Color.RED], [constant Vector2.ZERO][br]\r\n## - Enum link: [enum Node.ProcessMode], [enum Mesh.ArrayType][br]\r\n## - Annotation link: [annotation @GDScript.@export], [annotation @GDScript.@onready][br]\r\n## - Constructor link: [constructor Vector2.Vector2], [constructor Color.Color][br]\r\n## - Operator link: [operator Vector2.operator +], [operator Color.operator *][br]\r\n## - Theme item link: [theme_item Button.font], [theme_item Label.font_color][br]\r\n## - [lb]literal brackets[rb] with a [ClassName] for testing purposes.[br]\r\n## [br]\r\n## [u]Formatting:[/u] [s]strikethrough[/s], [color=red]red text[/color][br]\r\n## Press [kbd]Ctrl + S[/kbd] to save. Use [code]_ready()[/code] function.[br]\r\n## [br]\r\n## [center]Centered text[/center]\r\n## [br]\r\n## Basic code block:\r\n##\r\n## [codeblock]\r\n## func example():\r\n##     print(\"Hello World\")\r\n## [/codeblock]\r\n##\r\n## C# code block:\r\n##\r\n## [codeblock lang=csharp]\r\n## public void Example()\r\n## {\r\n##     GD.Print(\"Hello World\");\r\n## }\r\n## [/codeblock]\r\n##\r\n## Multiple language code blocks:\r\n##\r\n## [codeblocks]\r\n## [gdscript]\r\n## print(hash(\"a\")) # Prints 177670\r\n## [/gdscript]\r\n## [csharp]\r\n## GD.Print(GD.Hash(\"a\")); // Prints 177670\r\n## [/csharp]\r\n## [/codeblocks]\r\n##\r\n## Plain text block:\r\n##\r\n## [codeblock lang=text]\r\n## This is plain text\r\n## No syntax highlighting\r\n## [/codeblock]\r\n##\r\n## Parameter: Pass [param delta] for timing calculations.\r\n```\r\n  \r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\nHere's how things look in Zed right now with this PR:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"845\" height=\"364\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2025-07-18 16-57-28-min\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/42d8b3a7-c8fc-4dc0-a5d9-f6297e623f42\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"845\" height=\"364\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2025-07-18 16-57-38-min\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a135a6fb-0ed1-4012-857b-9f767638a485\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"845\" height=\"364\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2025-07-18 16-57-46-min\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0954f03b-0da3-4dbf-bff5-b63b044e4f14\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"879\" height=\"142\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2025-07-18 17-21-11-min\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bbdf17db-91dd-496b-9c9c-39260dd8439e\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3089878756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3091996287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3091996287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3091996287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64TB5_","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T07:35:13Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T07:35:13Z","body":"> An issue with the markdown parsing in code editors through the language server is that it seems fenced code blocks with a language are not supported. I will just get a literal ```gdscript if I try outputting that. That's why code blocks indent every line in the original code.\r\n\r\nI'm pretty sure this is an issue on our side. If I add this code:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n/** Format BBCode documentation from DocData to markdown */\r\nstatic String marked_documentation(const String &p_bbcode) {\r\n\treturn \"```gdscript\\nprint()\\n```\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nI get a correctly highlighted `print` at least in VSCode. I'd recommend checking whether the final markdown is valid, maybe there are linebreaks missing or there are some leading spaces that break the markdown?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3091996287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092146666","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3092146666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3092146666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64Tmnq","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T08:14:26Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T08:14:26Z","body":"That's right, makes sense, I'll remove the old code using indents then and get this working as intended.\r\n\r\nRegarding the [codeblocks][gdscript] syntax, any thoughts? We could perhaps look at the script path extension to only show the relevant language similar to how it's done in the Godot editor? I see the DocumentSymbol struct has the URI and path of the script - I could pass the extension to the markdown conversion function.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092146666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092164010","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3092164010","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3092164010,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64Tq2q","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T08:33:05Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T08:33:05Z","body":"That was due to a spacing issue in an older version of the code, now individual code listings will have syntax highlighting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092164010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092179016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3092179016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3092179016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64TuhI","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T08:49:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T08:49:25Z","body":"> I see the DocumentSymbol struct has the URI and path of the script - I could pass the extension to the markdown conversion function.\r\n\r\nThat's not really relevant is it? This fenced code blocks are undocumented syntax used exclusively by the builtin class ref. So in the normal use case there is no script associated with them. Also the language of the declaring file isn't really relevant. Assuming working language interop: when using a C# class from GDScript I'd be interested in GDScript examples even if the declaration is C#.\r\n\r\nSo I'd either show both or GDScript only, since users of the LSP will always be editing GDScript.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092179016/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092249348","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3092249348","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3092249348,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64T_sE","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T10:32:28Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T10:32:28Z","body":"You're right, thanks. I just added handling for the codeblocks part and preserved just the GDScript, similar to the editor docs - they seem to only show you the gdscript code or C# code contextually with this syntax.\r\n\r\nIt's now ready for review, feel free to either directly make or request any changes, whichever is more comfortable for you.\r\n\r\nI left the last 2 commits separate for now in case it helps break things down for review and will squash everything when needed","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092249348/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144857041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3144857041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3144857041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67crXR","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T14:53:53Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T14:56:40Z","body":"Thank you for the detailed review! I haven't had time to work on this since last week due to work, but I'll work on it tomorrow. No problem for adding a test case.\r\n\r\nDoes a single test that calls the function on multiple strings and checks that the markdown output of each call is as expected work for you? Or should something like this be split into smaller, individual unit tests? This way I can include the strings I have tested this on + the failing cases you mentioned in the review.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144857041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3146537987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3146537987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3146537987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67jFwD","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-02T14:26:28Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T14:26:28Z","body":"> Does a single test that calls the function on multiple strings and checks that the markdown output of each call is as expected work for you?\r\n\r\nYeah that's totally fine.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3146537987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161702926","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3161702926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3161702926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68c8IO","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T21:35:36Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T21:45:52Z","body":"I made sure to get a consistent result in both Zed and VSCode and to address and test the issues listed in last review in both editors.\r\n\r\nFor line returns, I went with paragraph markers, i.e. two line returns: `\\n\\n` (similarly to the existing implementation). The backslash variant ends up showing backslashes in Zed in a number of cases. So at least this works with the simple linewise conversion of bbcode to markdown the code uses. \r\n\r\nI checked codeblocks usage in the code reference and there's always a gdscript code listing (precisely, both gdscript and csharp code listings are present each time the [codeblocks] tag is used as far as I could see) so I did not add a fallback to the c# variant.\r\n\r\nThere's still one test string I need to clean up but I'll do it another day as it's getting late here. Just wanted to upload this as the code/functionality could use a second pair of eyes/hands in case there are important edge cases or issues remaining.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161702926/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3221362968","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3221362968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3221362968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AAhkY","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T18:46:31Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T18:46:31Z","body":"I just re-tested - built, ran test cases, tested docstrings manually in both Zed and VSCode. I couldn't spot issues (though it's quite possible that there are still a bunch of edge cases to catch). I had probably just missed a rebuild.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3221362968/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263931937","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3263931937","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497","id":3263931937,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ci6Yh","user":{"login":"NathanLovato","id":12694995,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjk0OTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12694995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanLovato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanLovato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-07T17:41:27Z","updated_at":"2025-09-07T17:41:27Z","body":"After looking at the macros used to check for unicode characters I went with just filtering out url (and / too) as you suggested. I tried adding a test case for this but it kept giving a false positive (see how the unicode characters get lost in the test output):\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n./modules/gdscript/tests/test_lsp.h:596: ERROR: CHECK_EQ( LSP::marked_documentation(\"Unicode class name [シーンマネージャー] with url: [url]https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/[/url]\"), \"Unicode class name [シーンマネージャー] with url: [https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/)\" ) is NOT correct!\r\n  values: CHECK_EQ( Unicode class name `ã·ã¼ã³ããã¼ã¸ã£ã¼` with url: [https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/), Unicode class name [シーンマネージャー] with url: [https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/) )\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you want a test case for this and know how to preserve the unicode chars in this context please let me know.\r\n\r\nI verified it worked manually instead:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2184\" height=\"596\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f33f2f2e-cd4e-495b-bf6f-589e15c84259\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263931937/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3289481112","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108497#issuecomment-3289481112","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108497",